# Example env file for `docker compose --env-file deploy.env up`.
# Copy to deploy.env and fill in. On the production box, cloud-init writes this file
# from terraform.tfvars (deploy/scaleway-relay/). ⚠ Production's copy also carries
# hand-added S3_*/BACKUP_S3_* lines the module cannot render (see its README), so
# never regenerate it from this example.
#
# Only three knobs: the rest of the relay's config (DEV_MODE=false, DATABASE_URL,
# BLOB_DIR) is hardcoded to safe prod defaults in docker-compose.yml.

# Hostname Caddy gets a TLS cert for and serves on. Must resolve (A record) to
# this host before the cert can be issued.
RELAY_DOMAIN=relay.tenshu.app

# Contact email for the Let's Encrypt account (cert-expiry notices).
ACME_EMAIL=admin@tenshu.app

# Comma-separated web origins allowed to call the relay cross-origin (web SDK +
# anonymous Mode-A share viewer). Empty => the relay's built-in apex default
# (https://tenshu.app + drive/control subdomains). Set this only if the web app
# is served from a different origin. A non-empty value REPLACES the default, so
# include the apex too if you still use it.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
